For each selected shared or value invocation, return one closed envelope with `outcome`, opaque `diagnostic`, and the requested complete schema_version 2 `manifest` on acceptance. The host extracts only that accepted manifest and submits it unchanged on stdin:
{{submit_steps|bullets}}
Do not execute these constructor commands or edit authority, ADR, handover, production or oracle files; DES is the sole authority writer. Return only the requested closed envelope, retaining every measured obligation above in an accepted manifest. Rejected or indeterminate envelopes omit `manifest` or set it to `null` and give a nonempty diagnostic naming the missing facts or finding and its remediation. A finding names `DEFECT-OWNER: <owner>`. The host alone submits accepted manifests and owns human interaction, further selected submissions and any constructor retry. Never return legacy provider facts, bare manifests, side-channel manifest files or DELIVERY-OUTCOME/NEXT summaries in place of the envelope; those summaries are DES observations after host submission, not your return contract.
If you cannot execute a DESIGN-required verification or lack an authorization or input, return `rejected` through the caller's enforced schema with `BLOCKED-BY: <owner>` in `diagnostic`, naming the precise prerequisite (for example `formal checks not authorized` or `checker unavailable at <path>`). Use a typed blocker field only if that schema provides it; leave the refused design payload null, never put a candidate manifest in `diagnostic`, and never return `accepted`.

